## 4. Verified Versioning Behavior

The initial object `ko-oba-001` was ingested as version `1` with lifecycle state `ACTIVE_USABLE`. A second request using the same version was rejected with HTTP 409, preventing an accidental overwrite.

The version `2` revision was then accepted. The previous version was archived as `SUPERSEDED_HISTORICAL`, while version `2` became the active usable representation. The active retrieval endpoint returned version `2`, preserved the previous-version reference, and returned the updated description and audit-trail note.

