## 7. Scope and Limitations

The Day 6 deliverable is a verified local SQLite/FastAPI OBA-ready backend. It demonstrates machine-consumable contracts, integrity safeguards, version history, active retrieval, provenance preservation, and relationship preservation. It is not yet a production deployment.

The implementation does not yet include authentication, authorization enforcement, database migrations, distributed locking, concurrency controls, external OBA integration, event publishing, asynchronous processing, or deployment configuration. The `validation_status` value is checked against `APPROVED` by the service safeguard but is not represented as a typed enum. The `previous_version_id` field is preserved as supplied and is not independently checked against a specific historical database row. These are follow-up hardening items and have not been represented as completed.

